   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to establishing a pilot\nprogram to create a non-crisis, quick assistance hotline for individuals with\nboth intellectual and developmental disabilities and/or complex behavioral\nneeds",
    "basePrintNo": "S6274",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6274-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13.17, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6274              Revised 5/13/2021\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to establishing a\npilot program to create a non-crisis, quick assistance hotline for indi-\nviduals with both intellectual and developmental disabilities and/or\ncomplex behavioral needs\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would provide general, non-medical, non-crisis assist-\nance to individuals with intellectual or developmental disabilities or\nbehavioral health concerns.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Creation of a 3 year pilot program by OPWDD for a 24/7\nhotline staffed by counselors for non-medical, non-crisis assistance to\nindividuals with developmental disabilities, in multiple languages.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would require OPWDD to create a 24 hour, seven days a\nweek hotline to answer questions that an individual with developmental\ndisabilities may have. Employees staffing the hotline would be trained\nto assist individuals with developmental disabilities for non-medical,\nnon-crisis related questions and issues. These counselors can provide\nhelp, guide and refer to services. This temporary program would be\nestablished for three years at which point its effectiveness could be\nevaluated.\n\nThe creation of this program will allow more individuals with develop-\nmental disabilities to live independently, with their family, or in a\nnon-traditional setting, while still having access to 24/7 assistance\nfor non-medical and non-crisis issues. Many individuals could live inde-\npendently with the right assistive and adaptive technology. This hotline\nis the first step in creating a continuum of services for individuals\nwith developmental disabilities to suit their needs.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
